      "title": "Several people injured after vehicle hits crowd in Newcastle waiting to farewell Knights team bus",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/03/several-people-injured-after-vehicle-hits-crowd-at-knights-grand-final-farewell-in-newcastle",
      "description": "<p>Driver arrested at the scene after a vehicle struck multiple people in a crowd</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A car has crashed into a crowd of people in Newcastle, injuring nine fans who were waiting to farewell the Knights team bus before the NRL grand final.</p><p>New South Wales police said that emergency services were called to Newcastle Link Road at the Transfield Drive roundabout in Wallsend about 9.30am on Saturday after reports a vehicle struck multiple people in a crowd.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/03/several-people-injured-after-vehicle-hits-crowd-at-knights-grand-final-farewell-in-newcastle\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-03T00:51:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "Magnitude 4.8 earthquake hits Victoria with tremors felt across Melbourne",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/02/magnitude-48-earthquake-hits-victoria-with-tremors-felt-across-melbourne",
      "description": "<p>The epicentre was at Leongatha, 130km south-east of Melbourne, with residents reporting houses shaking just after 2am</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A magnitude 4.8 earthquake struck Victoria in the early hours of Saturday morning, shaking Melbourne and waking people across the whole region.</p><p>Geoscience Australia said it <a href=\"https://earthquakes.ga.gov.au/\">detected</a> an earthquake with a preliminary magnitude of 4.8 at 2.01am near Leongatha, 130km south-east of Melbourne, with the tremors felt across the city’s eastern suburbs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/02/magnitude-48-earthquake-hits-victoria-with-tremors-felt-across-melbourne\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
